Found while building the rerank route (k92), present on main before it. add_node removes the node of the same id before it normalises the new one's `engine`; an unknown engine croaks after the removal, so a bad re-add (POST /skeid/nodes, nodes.add) takes the working node out of the inventory. k92 validates `rerank_format` before the removal; `engine` and the registry capacity block should be checked there too.

Wanted: every check in add_node that can croak runs before remove_node; a test that re-adds a node with an unknown engine and finds the old one still routable.

